ENTRY            C3131   20260520   20260819   20260819       C258
SUBENT        C3131001   20260520   20260819   20260819       C258
BIB                 12         45
TITLE      Study of the 25Mg(d,p)26Mg reaction to constrain the
           25Al(p,gamma)26Si resonant reaction rates in nova
           burning conditions
AUTHOR     (C.B.Hamill,P.J.Woods,D.Kahl,R.Longland,J.P.Greene,
           C.Marshall,F.Portillo,K.Setoodehnia)
REFERENCE  (J,EPJ/A,56,36,2020)
           #doi:10.1140/epja/s10050-020-00052-9
INSTITUTE  (2UK EDG,1USANCS,1USATNL,1USAANL)
           (2GERGER) European X-ray Free Electron Laser GmbH,
           Holzkoppel, 22869 Schenefeld, Germany
FACILITY   (VDGT,1USATNL) The 10-MV FN tandem Van de Graaff
           accelerator at the Triangle Universities Nuclear
           Laboratory (TUNL).
INC-SPECT  Beam currents on target varied between ~250-800 enA
           and were measured using a suppressed beam stop
           positioned at zero degrees.
DETECTOR   (SPEC,PROPC,SCIN) The TUNL high resolution Enge split-
           pole magnetic spectrograph accepted protons from the
           reactions, with an opening angle of 1.0 msr, which
           were then focused on to the spectrograph's focal
           plane. The positions of the momentum-dispersed
           particles on the focal plane were measured using two
           position sensitive avalanche counters. A dE/E
           detector combination, consisting of a gas
           proportionality counter to measure energy deposited,
           and a residual energy scintillator to measure total
           energy, allowed discrimination between different
           species of light ions.
SAMPLE     (12-MG-25,ENR=0.992) 25Mg targets enriched to a
           nominal isotopic composition of 99.2+-0.1%. The two
           targets used had thicknesses of 90 and 112 microg/cm2,
           measured using alpha particle energy loss
            (estimated uncertainty +-10%), and were backed by a
           thin gold flash.
METHOD     (EDE) Measurements of the reaction products were
           taken at multiple angles between 13-55 degrees.
           Excited states corresponding to the key states at
           5.691, 6.125 and 6.256 MeV in 26Mg were identified by
           a polynomial fit to well-known, strongly produced,
           states in 26Mg, with all observed peaks matching a
           known level of 26Mg within 5 keV.
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-S) The errors on the individual data points are
           statistical uncertainties.
STATUS     (APRVD) Approved by K.Setoodehnia on June 17, 2026.
HISTORY    (20260520C) BP
ENDBIB              45
